  "limitations": [
    "Small HRS scale (400 kg H2/d) with Indian cost and grid basis.",
    "Kinetic Table 1 is typographically malformed in the publisher PDF; reactor geometry, bed density, voidage cannot be read; beta of Eq. 2 not reported - rate law is not reproducible.",
    "Reactor pressure and PSA H2 recovery not stated in main text; NH3 prices (Fig. S6), CAPEX/OPEX/LCOH equations (Eqs. I-VII) and stream table (Table S2) only in SI (not available).",
    "Internal inconsistencies: recycled product gas composition 74.5 % N2/24.8 % H2 (likely transposed); PEMWE TCI share 95 % (text) vs 98.9 % (Fig. 5b); Scenario V NH3 OPEX share ~58 % (text) vs 51 % (Fig. 6); LCOH of Scenarios II and VI swapped in p. 9 text; CAPEX sensitivity magnitude implausible for 44 % compressor share.",
    "No NOx model; no uncertainty analysis; catalyst lifetime not stated."
  ],
  "relevance": "Aspen Plus (RKS-BM) model of a small fired NH3 cracker in which 18 % of product gas is burned as furnace fuel and product-gas heat preheats feed and air - a reference for AmCraX's tail-gas burner/heat-integration concept at small scale. Provides decentralised LCOH benchmarks (6.84-17.12 USD/kg H2 incl. NH3 supply, 350 bar; SMR 2.94) and cradle-to-gate GWP by NH3 origin (grey 17.91, solar PV 3.214, grid 112.79 kg CO2-eq/kg H2, India) for the environmental module, plus economic constants (electricity 80 USD/MWh, catalyst 24 USD/kg, 10 % discount, 20 yr, n = 0.8, CEPCI 2025 = 798.8). Kinetic constants should NOT be used."
}
